  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 350 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nPersistent upper level ridging will remain anchored southern plains \nThursday into the weekend. ENS/GEFS mean PWAT values are high during \nthis timeframe, as monsoonal/subtropical moisture aloft flows \nnorthward then turns east across the region on the northern \nperiphery of the upper high anchored to our south. ENS continues to \nsuggest PWAT values greater than 1.6\"...which would be exceeding the \nthe 90th percentile. As several waves/pertubations cross the area, \nrounds of showers and thunderstorms will be likely Thursday through \nSaturday. EFI index does suggest the potential for localized heavy \nrainfall Thursday. This seems reasonable with the abundance of \nmoisture that will be available. The locally heavy rain potential \nwill likely continue Friday and into Saturday as well. The 10/12Z \nENS mean QPF through Sunday has an average of around 1.5\" of \nrainfall area wide. The trends will definitely be monitored for this \npotential locally heavy rainfall event.  \n\nA considerable cool down is also expected Thursday through the \nweekend. This is primarily due to a considerable amount of cloud\ncover and easterly low-level flow. By Sunday, the low-levels \nbegin to dry out somewhat, as Canadian high pressure settles \nsouthward into the plains. Temperatures are expected to be below\nnormal during this timeframe, with highs in the 70s to lower \n80s.",
